<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:26Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>India: Delhi surpasses Lahore as world's most polluted city</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c0f917fa404bdc2559bf3831a1861a35b4fc7fbecafe65e389fd30315768beb1</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T06:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-delhi-surpasses-lahore-as-world-s-most-polluted-city/live-79946817--53d17bc3619e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-delhi-surpasses-lahore-as-world-s-most-polluted-city/live-79946817?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Delhi's Air Quality Index (AQI) was recorded to be higher than Lahore in Pakistan on Friday, which made it the most polluted city globally.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Gen Z protests: Do Baby Boomers really have it better than young people?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:41021e4251ab825b564fcf9b18942904f828e0e0265f3dc152cd04bdc937cef4</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T06:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gen-z-protests-do-baby-boomers-really-have-it-better-than-young-people/a-79918854--e581c42657a0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gen-z-protests-do-baby-boomers-really-have-it-better-than-young-people/a-79918854?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Should young people in Germany be more worried about their future than Baby Boomers were in the 1980s and 1990s? Or should both generations take to the streets and protest together? DW checked the data.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Senegal Youth Olympics in Dakar end on high note</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7945f3f15e55414e8d9d2ccfd2a23e8d830e959690fb9537e9c1c1b5e6c8e1af</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T04:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/senegal-youth-olympics-in-dakar-end-on-high-note/a-79944820--d8ec73fdda7d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/senegal-youth-olympics-in-dakar-end-on-high-note/a-79944820?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Enthusiastic crowds attended the games in Senegal, with China taking home the most gold medals. It's the first Olympic Games since Russia's war on Ukraine where Russian athletes can compete under their own flag.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Trump to meet Xi, Putin for three-way huddle on nuclear arms talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9c82df424e48c82d6b61b0428f88b447b1a36365e9a4d45ff547bbad9ce62601</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:59Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T04:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-to-meet-xi-putin-for-three-way-huddle-on-nuclear-arms-talks/a-79946408--68d06493f128.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-to-meet-xi-putin-for-three-way-huddle-on-nuclear-arms-talks/a-79946408?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The White House has said President Donald Trump will urge Xi Jinping and Vladimir Putin to discuss cutting nuclear arsenals in Shenzhen next week, though a senior US official expects no agreement.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>SpaceX launches Starship rocket, fails to recover booster</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a98b9f34d48aeb32ad092dd8e1672abad6bff46b36760b691171401ee3257b84</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T02:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spacex-launches-starship-rocket-fails-to-recover-booster/a-79946091--bd09d60b45a7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spacex-launches-starship-rocket-fails-to-recover-booster/a-79946091?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">SpaceX had planned to catch and later reuse both stages of its biggest rocket for the first time. But the booster exploded over the Gulf of Mexico, while the spacecraft continued into orbit.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US lifts nationwide ground stop for airports hours after halting all departures</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aaa8d1914f7700710f162baa4321da694be36b72e42936bf57dc6212790e8177</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T01:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-lifts-nationwide-ground-stop-for-airports-hours-after-halting-all-departures/a-79945062--ab4e85db51f9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-lifts-nationwide-ground-stop-for-airports-hours-after-halting-all-departures/a-79945062?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US federal aviation regulator has lifted a nationwide ground stop for all airports. Trump administration officials blame "overloaded" and "outdated" systems for the hourslong halt to departures.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Tanker collides with cruise ship on Mississippi in New Orleans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3035242843389995e3597d5bf67918d5cab47a462a1d4ad245287590790f78f6</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T21:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tanker-collides-with-cruise-ship-on-mississippi-in-new-orleans/a-79945080--29dd618b519d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tanker-collides-with-cruise-ship-on-mississippi-in-new-orleans/a-79945080?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A freighter collided with a cruise ship carrying around 130 people in New Orleans, causing the paddlewheel vessel to capsize. More than 30 people were hospitalized, but all passengers survived and were accounted for.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine updates: Europe to send united front to potential peace talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:04f0f3da6c8215db6f3a79250e55c25fc62853be9f8a86064dc0c5fba5d72925</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T19:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-updates-europe-to-send-united-front-to-potential-peace-talks/live-79937459--c475e3dc5244.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-updates-europe-to-send-united-front-to-potential-peace-talks/live-79937459?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany, France, the UK, Italy and Poland — as well as the EU itself — will jointly represent Europe in possible peace talks. Meanwhile, a second car bomb in two days has exploded in Moscow.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>David Walliams: UK police launch sex offense probe into comedian</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7cf7432218424a146f60faaa70f97d088fa3464c0f38f975088fcd502fed6a6e</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T19:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/david-walliams-uk-police-launch-sex-offense-probe-into-comedian/a-79944161--cffd271a388c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/david-walliams-uk-police-launch-sex-offense-probe-into-comedian/a-79944161?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The "Little Britain" star and "Britain's Got Talent" judge has been accused of engaging in sexual misconduct and inappropriate behavior towards young women and girls. Walliams denies the allegations.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo celebrates Mass in his former diocese of Chiclayo, Peru</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0e4bff89740cc127c3ec18b8c74abba398a40dc4b1df773054817affa953e11a</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T18:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pope-leo-celebrates-mass-in-his-former-diocese-of-chiclayo-peru/a-79944167--e8ccd3bfe138.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pope-leo-celebrates-mass-in-his-former-diocese-of-chiclayo-peru/a-79944167?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Over a million people have gathered for Mass with Pope Leo XIV on Friday. The event in northern Peru, where he served as bishop before becoming head of the Catholic Church, is the centerpiece of his South American tour.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>The dangers of revising Europe's security architecture</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d430c2cdb56b517a6a8bde7e024e1594cb8bbec6ef790a3d28d3d13afda55954</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T17:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-dangers-of-revising-europe-s-security-architecture/a-79943049--ae25152ee718.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-dangers-of-revising-europe-s-security-architecture/a-79943049?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Experts warn against revising Europe's security framework because they say it would mean granting Moscow its longstanding wish of renegotiating postwar security on the continent.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU leaders urged to 'act now' to stay AI competitive with US, China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e11d9b387b9398ecc9c2e783c6f8371defe410060a239c43fa7280b1db4ba473</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T16:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-leaders-urged-to-act-now-to-stay-ai-competitive-with-us-china/a-79937463--41561118bdc0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-leaders-urged-to-act-now-to-stay-ai-competitive-with-us-china/a-79937463?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">EU leaders in Dublin were called on by an AI executive to move quickly in the tech race with the US and China. EU official Metsola, however, expressed frustration with the idea that the bloc is behind in AI development.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>What's going on with the polar vortex?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:34372d20b6d0bd128659c053243af11a2f536e7a03bbc1aa317d4b201d6e74df</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T16:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-s-going-on-with-the-polar-vortex/a-79943105--6a28f0640609.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-s-going-on-with-the-polar-vortex/a-79943105?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Observations show the ring of fierce winds that rotate at the Earth's North Pole has changed direction. Scientists say it's a historic disruption and the earliest reversal on record. What could it mean for the weather?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Ice hockey: Russia threatens against Canada and Germany over exclusion from tournaments</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:09af6f7921e89ebdf21dc9fa6460c0d18acdb1a5676218c8abc6f1b5995cf4b1</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T16:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-russia-threatens-against-canada-and-germany-over-exclusion-from-tournaments/a-79942676--747c5baa6347.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-russia-threatens-against-canada-and-germany-over-exclusion-from-tournaments/a-79942676?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A fortnight after the CAS ordered ice hockey's governing body to reintegrate Russia into international play, a solution remains elusive. Now Russia has threatened to take legal action against two tournament hosts.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Why does El Salvador's Bukele have troops in Haiti?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f6063e2cc5d1775dcd5545d6d18c348eecb4398bde5c9b782d7f071dedd760a6</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T15:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-does-el-salvador-s-bukele-have-troops-in-haiti/a-79940771--dfce4a53e7c3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-does-el-salvador-s-bukele-have-troops-in-haiti/a-79940771?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Haiti's Prime Minister congratulating El Salvador's President for a gang crackdown in Haiti has shone a light on the relationship between the two countries. What's going on, and where does the US stand?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iran targeted US radar system in Bahrain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cb1a85a9c927dfc7b0ab3fc25c2bf5c338f9ff2df8ed7e103dcbfda9d41eebe8</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T15:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-targeted-us-radar-system-in-bahrain/a-79942640--6a6890129eef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-targeted-us-radar-system-in-bahrain/a-79942640?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iran claimed it struck US radar systems in Bahrain, while the US said it had intercepted the attacks. Clashes continue in the Strait of Hormuz, as the war remains in a state of de-escalation.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Beijing faces its Russia dilemma amid talk of Xi-Trump-Putin summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:39af6be7acbaf68465d50bf9290a800f9dd639296cfbdd6f0892e14a9c6659e0</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T15:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/beijing-faces-its-russia-dilemma-amid-talk-of-xi-trump-putin-summit/a-79942427--4d68b234d525.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/beijing-faces-its-russia-dilemma-amid-talk-of-xi-trump-putin-summit/a-79942427?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">China is forced to tread carefully as it considers hosting a meeting between Xi Jinping, Vladimir Putin, and Donald Trump. While the optics are sure to favor Moscow, Beijing is risking its image at the global stage.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Cyber attacks and hybrid warfare: Germany gives sweeping powers to its police and intelligence services</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9d274ea786678fcac968e19bd2a9f6c02d7bd5b6cb21b215f609c081f380b55c</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T15:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cyber-attacks-and-hybrid-warfare-germany-gives-sweeping-powers-to-its-police-and-intelligence-servic/a-79941507--8b38eb9f8681.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cyber-attacks-and-hybrid-warfare-germany-gives-sweeping-powers-to-its-police-and-intelligence-services/a-79941507?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Drone sightings and cyberattacks have heightened security concerns. How are the police preparing to meet these challenges? And how do intelligence services plan to counter threats from both domestic and foreign sources?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Indonesia's wiretapping scandal opens a political fault line</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f888db3ec8a2a3b3cf42d4c824fdc494c8812c56b2c4be2d537625c577bbb21</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T14:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/indonesia-s-wiretapping-scandal-opens-a-political-fault-line/a-79939753--0451bf449bfd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/indonesia-s-wiretapping-scandal-opens-a-political-fault-line/a-79939753?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Senior police officers are accused of illegally monitoring President Prabowo Subianto, exposing rival networks within Indonesia's security establishment and renewing concerns about political misuse of surveillance.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Is the AI bubble bursting just as Anthropic goes public?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:64ea71601b741faa16f123988b9f2f832d61576b44a609a94a7962a7cfb90ad1</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T12:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-the-ai-bubble-bursting-just-as-anthropic-goes-public/a-79896537--10f78cdc2264.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-the-ai-bubble-bursting-just-as-anthropic-goes-public/a-79896537?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The sharp sell-off in tech stocks after the US midterms has cast doubt on Anthropic's looming IPO. Yet with hundreds of billions still being invested, some think the AI party is still in full swing.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Nmecha won't repeat controversial goal celebration</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed70624bc63bbe5702de7c6c3bf70b5f1739fead46dff66390d618dbec307f98</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T11:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-nmecha-won-t-repeat-controversial-goal-celebration/a-79937994--cc5ab533247b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-nmecha-won-t-repeat-controversial-goal-celebration/a-79937994?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany head coach Jürgen Klopp says that midfielder Felix Nmecha will not repeat a goal celebration that sparked controversy over the past week. Germany are set to face Serbia and the Netherlands in the Nations League.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
